// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Contact Name : Roy Cooling 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Name :
"P1202890013" "Roy Cooling"
// ProfessionString :
"P1974235132" "FBSA Agent"
// DescriptionString :
"P72039738" "Roy Cooling is one of the top agents within the FBSA. He served for many years in the Marine Corps before being honorably discharged for valor in the field. He was recruited by the FBSA to help regulate super-powered affairs in Paragon City and to also do fieldwork when need be."
// LocationString :
// HelloString :
"P3070143890" "We've got ourselves a situation to handle, {HeroName}."
// HelloString :
"P1962764845" "Hold on, {HeroName}. Got the wife on my other phone. One second.<br><br>Yes... honey, look, I've got to go.<br><br>Sorry, {HeroName}. Let's get to work."
// HelloString :
"P887238024" "Hold on, {HeroName}. Got the wife on my other phone. One second.<br><br>No, look, I probably won't be back for dinner. I really need to get going, I'm sorry.<br><br>Sorry, {HeroName}. Let's get to work."
// HelloString :
"P1050982068" "Hold on, {HeroName}. Got the wife on my other phone. One second<br><br>I'm just saying, he had every right to punch the kid in the face. Why should <i>our</i> child get in trouble got defending himself? Look, I've got {HeroName} here, I need to call you back.<br><br>Sorry, {HeroName}, had a little trouble with our boy at school. Let's get to work."
// IDontKnowYouString :
"P1290433254" "Sorry kiddo, but I'm afraid I need someone I can trust to help me handle this current situation."
// NoTasksRemainingString :
"P3382728858" "We did some good work solving the whole medi-porter crisis, {HeroName}. If anything else happens, I'll let you know."
// PlayerBusyString :
"P2954052754" "You've got way too many issues to handle right now, {HeroName}. Finish up what you're doing and get back to me."
// ComeBackLaterString :
"P1836216375" "I've got some dangerous things to handle, kiddo. Come back and talk with me when you've reached security level 20."
// RelationshipChangeString_ToFriend :
"P138992395" "Let's keep moving on this whole crisis."
// RelationshipChangeString_ToConfidant :
// FailsafeLevelString :

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - DialogTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Praetorian Text :
"P950502307" "Well hey there {Hero.gender=male fella|miss}. I don't believe I've seen you around these parts too much. Name's Roy Cooling. I heard from the higher ups you're recently registered with the help of good 'ol Steve Sheridan.<br><br>Doesn't exactly say here where you're from, which makes me mighty curious as to what your origins are."
// Answer Text :
"P205695356" "I'm from Praetoria."
// Answer Text :
"P3010816006" "It doesn't matter. I'm here to help."
// Page ImPraetorian Text :
"P2491144287" "Praetoria? That's real interesting, kid. Now, you don't need to worry about me thinking you're the devil's right hand {Hero.gender=male pal|gal}. I know there's plenty of you folks from over yonder who want to give us good people of Primal Earth a hand, so I'm not going to try and stop you. Truth of the matter is that we're in a heap of trouble right now with that Emperor Cole trying to invade us, as I'm sure you're well aware of. What I'm about to tell you is classified top secret. Not even the PPD or Longbow know about this.<br><br>We've got word that Cole's invading armies have ways to disable our <color yellow>medi-porters</color>. Now, I don't think I need to tell you how out of hand this here thing could get if heroes start being wiped out in the streets. However, them folks at <color yellow>Medi-Corp</color> have a solution to Cole and his plan to whole-sale slaughter all of us good folks in Primal Earth. We've just got one small problem with all that."
// Answer Text :
"P2247846192" "What is the problem?"
// Page PraetorianWhereProblem Text :
"P279132415" "Well, being from Praetoria, you're probably not aware of this little controversy brewin' around these parts. See, only <color yellow>registered super powered heroes</color> receive medi-porters. This here has gotten a lotta normal folks pretty upset, seeing as how they feel this technology should be given to everyone. Now, that would be done if there weren't a lot of risks involved in it, which I won't get into right now.<br><br>Anyway, knowing that, Medi-Port Tech announced recently that they're upgrading those medi-porters to be 'more responsive'. 'Course, they're already as responsive as they're going to get, it's mainly the upgrade to make sure those Praetorians can't blast through our systems. The public got into an uproar and formed a group called the <color yellow>Citizens for Medi-Porters</color>. They started protestin' this action left and right. Now, we in the FBSA weren't too worried about it, until recently, when <color red>the finished tech to improve the medi-porters went missing.</color><br><br>Now, I assume you can see the problem we've got on our hands. Without that tech, your buddies in Praetoria are gonna march in here and zap down any super who isn't some sorta immortal or regeneration folk. That's why I'm here, and why I'm requesting your help, {HeroName}. We're going to track down this missing tech before things get out of hand. Are you ready?"
// Answer Text :
"P3053779715" "I'm ready. What's our first lead?"
// Page HidePraetorian Text :
"P216678927" "That's fine, if you don't want to tell. Plenty of suspicious super hero folk wandering around these places, what with groups like <color red>Malta</color> and all lurking in the shadows. Maybe down the road you'll give me a little trust about this whole matter, but we can worry about that later.<br><br>Right now, we've got ourselves into a whole heap of trouble regarding folks called <color yellow>Praetorians</color> looking to invade this here planet of ours. Normally, this wouldn't be a problem, seeing as how gettin' word that we're under the threat of an interdimensional invasion is called 'Tuesdays' here in the FBSA. Now, what I'm about to tell you is top secret, not even the PPD or Longbow are aware of this. Our current problem is that big bad Cole has got himself a way to bypass the medi-port system so that if a super gets shot in the chest, he ain't getting up afterwards.<br><br>Lucky for us, our boys in <color yellow>Medi-Corp</color> got us a solution for this. <i>Unlucky</i> for us, another problem went and crept up."
// Answer Text :
"P3711865331" "What happened?"
// Page HidePraetorianWhereProblem Text :
"P3090478041" "Well, here's the little set up. The regular folk around these parts can't get medi-porters, and that's causing a whole bit of uproar. Now, there's a ton of issues with giving everyone a medi-porter, issues that I won't get into, but suffice to say, if it could be done, it would've been. Anyway, there was an announcement some time ago by our boys working on the medi-porters that an upgrade was comin' along, one to make the system more responsive. Of course, it's gonna do a lot more than that; the new system is gonna be what we call 'Praetorian-proof', that way we'll have ourselves some backup against them devils in Praetoria.<br><br>Unfortunately, this caused an uproar in the populace of Paragon City, with a lotta folks saying that everyone should be getting the medi-porters first before any upgrades are done. There's even a group called <color yellow>Citizens for Medi-Porters</color> that was founded to lead the charge. This whole thing wouldn't be too bad, if it wasn't for the fact that just when the new tech was finished, it was <color red>stolen from the labs of Medi-Corp!</color><br><br>That's where you and I come in, kid. The FBSA is taking direct control over the situation, and they've assigned me to handle it. I could use someone who I can trust to help track down where this tech is and get it back to help all of you supers fight off Cole and his Praetorians. Are you in? "
// Answer Text :
"P302159535" "I'm in. What's our first move?"
// Page NotPraetorian Text :
"P1174195794" "Good to see you swung on by, {HeroName}. I've heard a whole lot about your efforts in making this city of ours a better place. Name's Roy Cooling, agent with the FBSA.<br><br><color orange>Roy displays his FBSA ID long enough for you to see that it's genuine.</color><br><br>I'm looking for the help of someone such as yourself with a little situation we've got ourselves into regarding the <color yellow>Praetorians</color>. Well, it's a bit more than those Praetorians. Mainly, it's got to do with the <color yellow>medi-port system</color> that all you supers rely on. You may or may not be aware about the whole controversy going on with it. See, a lot of regular folks around here in Paragon are ticked that they don't have medi-porters. It wasn't too much of a problem earlier on, but now that we've had it for a few years, people are wondering why it hasn't been put out to the public.<br><br>Now, there's a lot of reasons <i>why</i> we can't have it in the hands of the public, pretty serious ones too. I won't go into them, but I want to assure you that if the folks over at <color yellow>Medi-Corp</color> could have this technology in the hands of everyone, they would."
// Answer Text :
"P508254840" "Alright, so what is the issue?"
// Page WhatIssue Text :
"P3104071181" "Issue we got ourselves into is two-fold. You should know right away, this information I'm telling you is top secret, not even the PPD or Longbow know about this.<br><br>Now, those Praetorians, they've got enough tech that they figured out a way to disable our medi-port systems when they invade. This means that anyone who isn't some sort of immortal or indestructible machine is gonna die when this war starts. That's something we gotta make sure we avoid. The good folks over at Medi-Corp devised an upgrade to the medi-porters to prevent this and put an announcement out that a 'stability upgrade' was coming out for the system.<br><br>It's too bad for us they did. To be honest, if they had let the FBSA know earlier, we would've told them not to announce anything. Now, we've got a PR nightmare on our hands. The public outcry about medi-porters not being granted to everyone is louder than ever, with a group called <color yellow>Citizens for Medi-Porters</color> being formed. I wouldn't be too worried about this, if it weren't for the fact that the new tech that was made <color red>is now missing.</color> The one thing that's protecting us from being stomped by those Praetorians is <i>gone</i>.<br><br>That's why the FBSA has sent me to personally look into the situation, and why I've asked for your help, {HeroName}. We've got to work together to track down the missing tech and get it back to our boys before it's too late for all those supers going to fight against the Praetorians!"
// Answer Text :
"P1086245786" "I'm ready to help. What's the first move?"
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 


